        "original_id": "91342b69-a03d-5ffb-9e32-9edfdcf35bff",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: American Scientist, Dwell, Global Open Access Forum\n- Organizations: Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society\n- People: Lara Hedberg Deam, Karrie Jacobs\n- Concepts: Open Access\n\nFacts:\n- American Scientist has been published since 1913 by Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society.\n- American Scientist is an American bimonthly science and technology magazine, and it is informally abbreviated AmSci.\n- The Global Open Access Forum was created in September 1998 by American Scientist, which is published by Sigma Xi.\n- The Global Open Access Forum was originally called the September98-Forum, and it was created before the term Open Access was coined.\n- Dwell was launched with a magazine in September 2000 to bridge the gap between design professionals and enthusiasts.\n- Lara Hedberg Deam launched Dwell, and Karrie Jacobs served as its Editor-in-Chief.",
